{
  "_comment": [
    "Adaptation to per-limb / per-joint dynamics shifts on Hopper-v4, Ant-v4, Humanoid-v4: 18M steps per run, 3 seeds,",
    "no baselines (the 24M run `trillium_dynamics_3env_24m.json` is the baseline: same seeds 18606, 16858, 63790, same",
    "hyperparameters). Companion of `trillium_dynamics_shifts_18m.json` (global shifts) with the same layout:",
    "20 experiments x 3 envs x 3 seeds = 180 runs on one 192-core node, ~10-12.5 h.",
    "Two-segment runs switch at 9M; three-segment runs switch at 6M and 12M.",
    "Shift types (none of them used before):",
    "  mass_rand     every body's mass (and inertia) x a factor drawn log-uniformly from [0.5, 2]",
    "  friction_rand every limb geom's sliding friction x [0.3, 2]; the floor is set to 0.3 so that the limb's own value",
    "                governs each contact (MuJoCo takes the max of the two touching geoms' friction)",
    "  damping_rand  every joint's damping x [0.33, 3]",
    "  gear_rand     every actuator's gear (motor strength) x [0.5, 1.5]",
    "  limb_heavy    one limb's bodies x 3 (Hopper thigh / foot, Ant front-left / back-right leg, Humanoid right / left leg)",
    "The random factors are drawn once (numpy seed 20261026) and written into this file as absolute values, so every seed",
    "and every experiment using 'draw A' of a type sees exactly the same model; 'draw B' is an independent second draw.",
    "Values are per env (each has its own body/geom/joint/actuator names), so all experiments are given through `per_env`.",
    "Named mods set absolute values; a `*_scale: 1.0` resets that whole field to the original model, which is how a",
    "condition is undone when going back to base or switching to a different type.",
    "Groups: 1-7 base -> new world (5 single types, 2 compounds); 8-12 shifted world -> base;",
    "13-20 three segments (there-and-back, re-randomisation A -> B of the same type, switches between types, and the",
    "heavy limb moving to a different limb).",
    "Videos: n_eval episodes every video_every steps, at each switch (just before it) and at the end.",
    "Model snapshots every 1M steps and at the end."
  ],

  "defaults": {
    "N": 18000000,
    "seeds": [18606, 16858, 63790],
    "gamma": 0.99,
    "beta1": 0.0,
    "normalize_obs": true,
    "pnorm": true,
    "scaled_td": true,
    "n_eval": 2,
    "video_every": 3000000,
    "save_model": true,
    "save_model_every": 1000000
  },

  "envs": {
    "Hopper-v4": {"actor_lr": 1.1e-05, "critic_lr": 7.7e-05, "alpha_lr": 0.3},
    "Ant-v4": {"actor_lr": 0.0063, "critic_lr": 0.0087, "alpha_lr": 0.07},
    "Humanoid-v4": {"actor_lr": 0.0063, "critic_lr": 0.0087, "alpha_lr": 0.07}
  },

  "experiments": [
    {"name": "base_to_mass_rand",
     "_": "1. base for 9M, then every body mass x [0.5, 2] (draw A)",
     "per_env": {
       "Hopper-v4": {
         "schedule": [{"step": 9000000, "mods": {"mass": {"torso": 2.451, "thigh": 2.13, "leg": 2.136, "foot": 7.611}}}]
       },
       "Ant-v4": {
         "schedule": [{"step": 9000000, "mods": {"mass": {"torso": 0.2863, "front_left_leg": 0.06997, "aux_1": 0.03789, "4": 0.03436, "front_right_leg": 0.02896, "aux_2": 0.03811, "7": 0.04068, "back_leg": 0.02084, "aux_3": 0.02546, "10": 0.04626, "right_back_leg": 0.04867, "aux_4": 0.04634, "13": 0.05869}}}]
       },
       "Humanoid-v4": {
         "schedule": [{"step": 9000000, "mods": {"mass": {"torso": 8.98, "lwaist": 3.985, "pelvis": 12.25, "right_thigh": 2.848, "right_shin": 1.469, "right_foot": 2.876, "left_thigh": 9.154, "left_shin": 1.826, "left_foot": 1.746, "right_upper_arm": 2.79, "right_lower_arm": 1.003, "left_upper_arm": 3.245, "left_lower_arm": 0.7329}}}]
